ur4|n|Anything given; anything voluntarily transferred by one person to another without compensation; a present; an offering. ; The act, right, or power of giving or bestowing; as, the office is in the gift of the President. ; A bribe; anything given to corrupt. ; Some quality or endowment given to man by God; a preeminent and special talent or aptitude; power; faculty; as, the gift of wit; a gift for speaking. ; A voluntary transfer of real or personal property, without any consideration. It can be perfected only by deed, or in case of personal property, by an actual delivery of possession. ; To endow with some power or faculty.	a:1vhw,31,7~1vhw,31,7	N:yhg,97,5;arv,58,6;bnb,55,2;tpa,14,2~arv,58,6;yhg,97,5;bnb,55,2;tpa,14,2
